<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  launchd USER AGENT for the `save` daemon (macOS autostart).

  This is a LaunchAgent (~/Library/LaunchAgents, loaded into the gui/<uid>
  domain), NOT a LaunchDaemon (/Library/LaunchDaemons, the system domain).
  That distinction is load-bearing, for two reasons:

    1. Keychain and OAuth. An agent runs as you, inside your login session,
       with access to your home directory and your config dir.

    2. Dataless-file materialization. If archive_root lives in iCloud Drive
       (or any other FileProvider), macOS may EVICT archived files with
       "Optimize Mac Storage" on, leaving placeholders whose bytes come back
       only when something reads them. Whether a read is allowed to pull them
       back is a per-process I/O policy that is INHERITED FROM THE PARENT
       (see setiopolicy_np(3), IOPOL_TYPE_VFS_MATERIALIZE_DATALESS_FILES).
       The system default is OFF, and a job in the system domain inherits
       that: a LaunchDaemon reading an evicted file gets EDEADLK instead of
       the file's contents. A GUI-session agent inherits the session's
       policy, which is ON, so reads work. Run save as an agent.

       If you must run it in a context where materialization is off, launchd
       has an escape hatch — add to this dict:

           <key>MaterializeDatalessFiles</key>
           <true/>

       …and be aware that it turns every stray read into a network download.
       `save verify` deliberately goes the other way: it pins its own policy
       OFF and skips evicted files, unless you ask for them with its
       "materialize" flag.

  NOTE ON XML COMMENTS: a double hyphen is illegal inside one, which is why
  command-line flags are named without their leading dashes above.

  KeepAlive restarts the daemon if it ever exits (crash, `save` upgrade,
  transient failure); combined with save's own crash-safe write ordering
  and startup healing this is safe at any kill point. The daemon holds a
  single-instance flock, so a concurrent manual `save sync` is refused
  rather than corrupting anything.

  Install:
    1. Edit the ProgramArguments path below to where your `save` binary
       lives (e.g. /opt/homebrew/bin/save or $HOME/go/bin/save — launchd
       does not expand ~ or $PATH).
    2. cp docs/launchd/com.user.save.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    3. launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.user.save.plist

  Stop / uninstall:
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.user.save

  Logs go to ~/Library/Logs/save.log (adjust below; launchd creates the
  file, but the ~/Library/Logs directory must exist).
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.user.save</string>

	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/usr/local/bin/save</string>
		<string>run</string>
	</array>

	<!-- Restart whenever the process exits, for any reason. -->
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<true/>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>

	<!-- Don't restart-loop faster than every 30s if something is badly wrong. -->
	<key>ThrottleInterval</key>
	<integer>30</integer>

	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Background</string>

	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/Users/CHANGE_ME/Library/Logs/save.log</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/Users/CHANGE_ME/Library/Logs/save.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
